{"ticker":"HWM","updated":"2026-10-30T22:53:01Z","profile":{"longName":"Howmet Aerospace Inc.","shortName":"Howmet Aerospace Inc.","sector":"Industrials","industry":"Aerospace & Defense","country":"United States","website":"https://www.howmet.com","fullTimeEmployees":25430,"marketCap":79449219072,"trailingPE":42.935345,"forwardPE":30.201826,"priceToSalesTrailing12Months":8.164548,"pegRatio":0.8,"targetMeanPrice":322.15,"targetHighPrice":377.0,"targetLowPrice":255.0,"numberOfAnalystOpinions":20,"recommendationKey":"strong_buy","revenueGrowth":0.294,"earningsGrowth":0.495,"grossMargins":0.36625,"operatingMargins":0.2882,"profitMargins":0.21098,"totalRevenue":9731000320,"beta":null,"fiftyTwoWeekHigh":310.0,"fiftyTwoWeekLow":183.52,"currency":"USD","exchange":"NYQ","quoteType":"EQUITY","dividendYield":0.27},"summary":"Howmet Aerospace Inc. provides advanced engineered solutions for the aerospace and transportation industries in the United States, Japan, France, Germany, the United Kingdom, Mexico, Italy, Canada, Poland, China, and internationally. It operates through four segments: Engine Products, Fastening Systems, Engineered Structures, and Forged Wheels. The Engine Products segment offers airfoils and seamless rolled rings primarily for aircraft engines and industrial gas turbines; and rotating and structural parts. The Fastening Systems segment produces aerospace fastening systems, as well as commercial transportation, industrial, and other fasteners; and latches, bearings, fluid fittings, and installation tools. The Engineered Structures segment provides titanium ingots and mill products, aluminum and nickel forgings, and machined components and assemblies for aerospace and defense applications; and titanium forgings, extrusions, and forming and machining services for airframe, wing, aero-engine, and landing gear components. The Forged Wheels segment offers forged aluminum wheels and related products for heavy-duty trucks and commercial transportation markets. The company was formerly known as Arconic Inc. Howmet Aerospace Inc. was founded in 1888 and is based in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.","summary_zh":"Howmet Aerospace Inc. 為美國、日本、法國、德國、英國、墨西哥、義大利、加拿大、波蘭、中國和國際上的航空航太和運輸業提供先進的工程解決方案。該公司透過四個部門運作：引擎產品部門、緊固系統部門、工程結構部門和鍛造車輪部門。發動機產品部門主要為飛機發動機和工業燃氣渦輪機提供翼型件和無縫軋製環；以及旋轉部件和結構部件。緊固系統部門生產航太緊固系統以及商業運輸、工業和其他緊固件；以及閂鎖、軸承、流體配件和安裝工具。工程結構部門為航空航太和國防應用提供鈦錠和銑削產品、鋁和鎳鍛件以及機械加工零件和組件；以及機身、機翼、航空發動機和起落架部件的鈦鍛件、擠壓件以及成型和機械加工服務。鍛造車輪部門為重型卡車和商業運輸市場提供鍛造鋁輪和相關產品。該公司前身為 Arconic Inc.。 Howmet Aerospace Inc. 成立於 1888 年，總部位於賓州匹茲堡。","sector_zh":"工業","industry_zh":"航空航太與國防","candles":[{"t":"2025-09-02","o":172.31,"h":173.59,"l":170.81,"c":173.22,"v":1995200},{"t":"2025-09-03","o":173.4,"h":174.51,"l":172.41,"c":174.49,"v":1678700},{"t":"2025-09-04","o":174.87,"h":180.95,"l":174.66,"c":179.53,"v":2265600},{"t":"2025-09-05","o":180.25,"h":181.39,"l":173.38,"c":178.2,"v":2016700},{"t":"2025-09-08","o":178.28,"h":180.55,"l":178.28,"c":179.43,"v":1777300},{"t":"2025-09-09","o":178.78,"h":179.49,"l":176.32,"c":178.98,"v":1399600},{"t":"2025-09-10","o":180.0,"h":184.23,"l":179.62,"c":183.8,"v":1995500},{"t":"2025-09-11","o":184.39,"h":185.66,"l":181.36,"c":184.21,"v":2000200},{"t":"2025-09-12","o":185.0,"h":187.26,"l":184.5,"c":185.77,"v":1817100},{"t":"2025-09-15","o":186.0,"h":189.5,"l":186.0,"c":189.25,"v":1813200},{"t":"2025-09-16","o":189.5,"h":190.29,"l":186.47,"c":187.46,"v":3287800},{"t":"2025-09-17","o":187.58,"h":188.25,"l":183.24,"c":185.39,"v":2227600},{"t":"2025-09-18","o":184.67,"h":192.25,"l":182.78,"c":191.84,"v":2223200},{"t":"2025-09-19","o":192.9,"h":192.99,"l":186.3,"c":190.23,"v":4621000},{"t":"2025-09-22","o":192.5,"h":192.8,"l":190.0,"c":192.15,"v":2111200},{"t":"2025-09-23","o":192.45,"h":194.35,"l":189.72,"c":193.58,"v":2224900},{"t":"2025-09-24","o":194.56,"h":194.69,"l":190.09,"c":190.22,"v":1772200},{"t":"2025-09-25","o":189.53,"h":190.37,"l":186.73,"c":189.85,"v":1326900},{"t":"2025-09-26","o":192.0,"h":194.89,"l":191.13,"c":193.15,"v":2339400},{"t